# .dockerignore (repo root)
#
# Build-context exclusions for
# `docker build -f apps/web/Dockerfile .` - the
# build the VOC-032-T03 task defines and
# VOC-032-TEST-08 exercises. This file is
# consulted ONLY when the build context is the
# repo root, which is currently the case for the
# web Dockerfile only - the apps/api Dockerfile
# uses apps/api/ as its build context and is
# governed by apps/api/.dockerignore instead, not
# this one. Any future Docker build that uses the
# repo root as its context will inherit these
# exclusions; if such a build needs something
# excluded here, prefer adding a more specific
# .dockerignore at the relevant sub-tree rather
# than relaxing this one.

# Version control and build context metadata.
# `.git/` is the obvious one (never bake git
# history into an image); `.gitattributes` is
# pulled in transitively by some tools and is
# not needed in the build; `.github/` holds the
# workflows (none of which the image needs -
# CI runs them on a separate runner).
.git/
.gitattributes
.github/

# Dependency installations. pnpm writes the
# workspace's `node_modules/` trees during the
# build stage's `pnpm install` step; they are
# not part of the build CONTEXT and must not
# pollute it (re-including them would either
# make COPY copy them uselessly or, worse,
# shadow the freshly-installed deps).
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# Build outputs and dependency caches. The
# apps/api binary, the apps/web .next/ tree,
# pnpm's content-addressable store, and any
# compiled workspace package dist/ trees are
# all produced by their own build steps, not
# consumed as build-context input. apps/web/-
# playwright-report/, apps/web/test-results/,
# and apps/web/lighthouse-reports/ are runtime
# test artifacts (also gitignored, but
# re-asserted here for the build context).
apps/api/
apps/web/.next/
apps/web/playwright-report/
apps/web/test-results/
apps/web/lighthouse-reports/
.pnpm-store/
packages/*/dist/

# Non-build documentation. The web image does
# not need docs/, infra/, specs/, or the
# karsift-ai-infra submodule's own source.
# apps/web/scripts/ is excluded because the
# only thing in it - generate-tokens-css.mjs -
# is invoked at development time only and its
# generated output is already committed at
# apps/web/src/app/tokens.generated.css.
docs/
infra/
specs/
karsift-ai-infra/
.karsift/
tooling/
apps/web/scripts/

# Test-only files. apps/web/tests/ and the
# Playwright config are not part of the
# production build.
apps/web/tests/
apps/web/playwright.config.ts

# Local-only configuration. `.env*` matches
# .env, .env.local, .env.production, etc. - any
# of which a developer machine or staging host
# might drop into the working tree. They are
# never part of a Docker build context. Note
# this also matches apps/web/.env.example and
# apps/api/.env.example; that is intentional -
# neither is loaded by Next.js or pnpm at build
# time, and excluding them keeps the context
# tight. Both .env.example files remain in the
# source tree via the normal `COPY apps/web`
# step in the Dockerfile (which is a different
# source than this exclusion list applies to
# for the apps/web/ subtree, but .env* is
# still excluded by this rule; the Dockerfile
# does not COPY .env.example into the runtime
# image and the apps/web/ build step doesn't
# read it).
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Editor and OS noise. Mirrors the apps/api/
# .dockerignore's intent for the web build's
# context too.
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
*.swp
